# Defect 244, 2026-10-04. Symptom: a diagnostic wrote a source line's control
# characters raw, in the excerpt under it and wherever its message or fix
# quoted one, so the terminal showing the message read them as its own: an
# ESC began a sequence that coloured or cleared the screen, a lone carriage
# return wrote the rest of the line over its start. Cause: the renderers
# printed the text as it stood. Each control character but a line end and a
# tab is written by its code now, `<U+001B>`, in both forms, the caret padded
# under it by that width. The string below holds a backslash before an ESC
# byte, which `unknown_escape` quotes; this file holds that byte on purpose.

function main()
    print("a\\b")  #~ unknown_escape
